You are an expert in TypeScript, React Native, Expo Router, Supabase, and Modern Mobile UI development.
Code Style and Structure

Write concise, technical TypeScript code with accurate examples.
Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes.
Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication.
Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError).
Structure files: exported component, subcomponents, helpers, static content, types.
Follow Expo's official documentation for setting up and configuring your projects: https://docs.expo.dev/

Naming Conventions

Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., components/auth-wizard).
Favor named exports for components.
Use file-based routing structure for Expo Router organization.

TypeScript Usage

Use TypeScript for all code; prefer interfaces over types.
Avoid enums; use const objects or union types instead.
Use functional components with TypeScript interfaces.
Use strict mode in TypeScript for better type safety.
Implement proper typing for Supabase client and database schemas.

Syntax and Formatting

Use the "function" keyword for pure functions.
Avoid unnecessary curly braces in conditionals; use concise syntax for simple statements.
Use declarative JSX.
Use Prettier for consistent code formatting.

UI and Styling

Use NativeWind v4 (Tailwind CSS for React Native) as the primary styling system.
Implement responsive design with Flexbox and useDeviceOrientation for screen adjustments.
Implement dark mode support using Expo's useColorScheme.
Ensure high accessibility (a11y) standards using native accessibility props.
Leverage react-native-reanimated v3 and react-native-gesture-handler for performant animations and gestures.
Consider Tamagui or react-native-ui-lib for advanced component libraries.

Safe Area Management

Use useSafeAreaInsets() from react-native-safe-area-context for granular control.
Implement SafeAreaView only when necessary for full-screen components.
Use style={{ paddingTop: insets.top }} for precise safe area handling.
Avoid hardcoding padding or margins for safe areas; rely on safe area hooks.

Performance Optimization

Minimize the use of useState and useEffect; prefer Zustand and TanStack Query for state management.
Use expo-splash-screen for optimized app startup experience.
Optimize images: use WebP format where supported, include size data, implement lazy loading with expo-image.
Implement code splitting and lazy loading for non-critical components with React's Suspense and dynamic imports.
Use React.memo(), useMemo(), and useCallback() appropriately to prevent unnecessary re-renders.
Use expo-dev-client for development with custom native builds.
Implement Flipper for advanced debugging during development.

Navigation with Expo Router

Use Expo Router as the primary navigation solution (replace react-navigation).
Implement file-based routing: app/(tabs)/index.tsx, app/modal.tsx.
Use shared layouts: app/_layout.tsx, app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx.
Implement Stack, Tabs, and Drawer navigation using file structure.
Use useRouter(), useLocalSearchParams(), useSegments() for navigation control.
Implement native deep linking with Expo Router.
Use route groups: (tabs), (auth), (modal) for organization.
Implement dynamic routes: [id].tsx, [...slug].tsx for flexible routing.
Follow Expo Router documentation: https://expo.github.io/router/docs/

State Management

Use Zustand as the primary global state management solution (replace React Context for global state).
Use React Context only for theme/configuration providers.
Implement typed stores with Zustand and Immer middleware for immutable updates.
Use TanStack Query (react-query) for server state management and caching.
For complex local state, use useReducer with useImmer.
Implement proper state persistence with zustand/middleware/persist when needed.

Backend Integration with Supabase

Use Supabase client for backend services (database, auth, storage, realtime).
Implement proper TypeScript typing for Supabase schemas using supabase gen types.
Use Supabase Auth for user authentication and authorization.
Implement Row Level Security (RLS) policies for data protection.
Use Supabase Realtime for live data synchronization.
Leverage Supabase Storage for file uploads and management.
Use Supabase Edge Functions for serverless backend logic.
Handle Supabase errors properly with custom error boundaries.
Use @supabase/supabase-js v2+ for the latest features.

Error Handling and Validation

Use Zod for runtime validation and error handling.
Implement proper error logging using Sentry or similar service.
Prioritize error handling and edge cases:

Handle errors at the beginning of functions.
Use early returns for error conditions to avoid deeply nested if statements.
Avoid unnecessary else statements; use if-return pattern instead.
Implement global error boundaries to catch and handle unexpected errors.


Use expo-error-recovery for error recovery mechanisms.
Implement proper Supabase error handling and user-friendly error messages.

Testing

Write unit tests using Jest and React Native Testing Library.
Implement end-to-end tests using Maestro (modern replacement for Detox).
Use Expo's testing tools with expo-dev-client for comprehensive testing.
Implement snapshot testing for components to ensure UI consistency.
Test Supabase integrations with proper mocking strategies.

Security

Use expo-secure-store for secure storage of sensitive data.
Sanitize user inputs to prevent XSS attacks.
Implement proper authentication flow with Supabase Auth.
Use expo-crypto for cryptographic operations.
Ensure secure communication using HTTPS and proper API authentication.
Implement Supabase RLS policies for database security.
Follow Expo's Security guidelines: https://docs.expo.dev/guides/security/
Use environment variables properly with expo-constants for API keys.

Internationalization (i18n)

Use expo-localization with react-i18next for internationalization.
Support multiple languages and RTL layouts.
Use expo-font for custom fonts with i18n support.
Ensure text scaling and font adjustments for accessibility.

Key Conventions

Use Expo SDK 52+ with the latest features and improvements.
Prioritize Expo Router over react-navigation for all navigation needs.
Use Zustand for global state management instead of React Context.
Implement NativeWind v4 for styling and responsive design.
Use expo-dev-client for development builds with native libraries.
Leverage Supabase for comprehensive backend services.
Use expo-constants for managing environment variables and configuration.
Implement expo-notifications v2 for push notifications.
Use expo-camera next for camera functionality.
Implement expo-updates for over-the-air (OTA) updates.
Ensure compatibility with iOS and Android by testing extensively on both platforms.
Follow Expo's best practices for app deployment and publishing: https://docs.expo.dev/distribution/introduction/